kind check-if
title Check if a look uses the font set you expect.
intro A look's card shows its font set, and Enter on the Font set line lists the font sets with the look's own ticked. Picking the ticked one again changes nothing.
see looks/change-the-font-set-of-a-look
waits-for audit 1: a pick that changes nothing counts as a change not saved

file etc/vtium.conf
    version = 1
    font-name = unifont
    [look plain]
    font-name = mono
    [head console]
    vt = 5
    look = plain
file etc/batch.conf
    ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf
font fonts/mono.bdf 8x16
frit mono
    source=bdf:ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf

1. Go to the Looks tab.
2. Choose plain.
3. Choose Font set.
4. Choose mono.
5. Press Esc.
at the Looks tab
check screen lacks "not saved"
check screen lacks "look set plain --frit mono"
